               'item to a ref tip, a commit or a set of files, resolved now. A correction names '
               'the item it supersedes. Repeating the same key and request replays its receipt.\n'
               '\n'
               'OPTIONS AND ARGUMENTS\n'
               '    --root ROOT — required; Explicit fleet root.\n'
               '    --as NODE — required; Registered active node raising the item.\n'
               '    --kind {approval,question,review} — required; review, approval or question.\n'
               '    --title TEXT — required; One visible line within 256 UTF-8 bytes.\n'
               '    --detail TEXT — Optional visible line within 2048 UTF-8 bytes.\n'
               '    --repository PATH — Absolute path of the checkout the item is about.\n'
               '    --ref REF — Branch or ref whose tip the item is bound to.\n'
               '    --commit SHA — Full commit id the item is bound to; defaults to the ref tip.\n'
               '    --path PATH — repeatable; Repository-relative file the item is about.\n'
               '    --supersedes ID — Exact ID of the item this one corrects; it must be the head '
               'of its chain.\n'
               '    --idempotency-key KEY — required; Stable key for this exact request.\n'
               '\n'
               'OPERATION NOTES\n'
               '    With --ref the item goes stale when the ref moves; with --path as well, only '
               'when a named file changes. With only --path the item goes stale when a named '
               "file's bytes change. --path with --commit alone is refused.\n"
